  "note": "Triennial election of the county council, 1911: polled Wednesday 31 May 1911 in six divisions; the other fifteen were returned unopposed. Two seats. The outgoing members were H. G. MacGeagh, D.L., who did not seek re-election (his nomination was withdrawn), and John Mahaffy. Result declared by Fred. W. Pollock, returning officer. No party labels printed."
